    \item $G$: positive semi-definite symmetric $r \times r$ matrix.
    \item $D$: $s \times s$ diagonal matrix.
    \item $A, U, B, V$: submatrices making up a general linear method.
    \item $r$: number of rows/columns in $G$ and $V$.
    \item $s$: number of rows/columns in $D$, $A$, and $B$.
\end{itemize}

Referenced equations:
